# Auto-generated by opencode-vm — safe to edit; regenerated only if missing.
#
# Why these are ignored by default:
#   cache/         Incremental-build cache (tree-sitter parses + file hashes).
#                  Easily 10,000+ files on medium codebases — VSCode will warn
#                  "too many active changes". Reproduced automatically by
#                  `graphify watch`/`update`; committing it trades severe repo
#                  bloat for marginal cold-start speedup. Always skip.
#   manifest.json  Tracks mtime per source file. Per graphify upstream, mtimes
#                  are not preserved across `git clone`, so a committed
#                  manifest forces a full rebuild on every fresh checkout
#                  anyway — better to regenerate locally.
#   graph.json     The full queryable graph. Real-world mcrepos produce graphs
#                  >100 MB (single .json file), which exceeds GitHub's hard
#                  cap per file. Each `opencode-vm` session rebuilds it via
#                  the in-VM watcher — fresh on session start is fine.
#   graph.html     Interactive visualization, large and binary-ish; same
#                  rebuild-on-session story.
#
# What stays committed (and is what PR reviewers actually read):
#   GRAPH_REPORT.md   — human-readable summary of god-nodes + cross-repo
#                       connections. Typically <1 MB. Diff-able in PRs.
#   README.md         — explains this folder's purpose to humans.
#   .gitignore        — this file.
#
# If your codebase is small enough that graph.json fits comfortably in git
# (<25 MB rule of thumb), feel free to remove `graph.json` from this file —
# committing it makes a fresh clone instantly query-ready without waiting
# for the watcher's initial pass.

cache/
manifest.json
graph.json
graph.html
